# .dockerignore — TASK-030
#
# Keeps the build context small, reproducible and free of anything that could
# either bloat the image, leak a secret, or defeat build caching. The build
# stage needs only go.mod/go.sum and the Go source tree; everything below is
# either irrelevant to `go build ./cmd/mcpmock` or actively unwanted in a
# build context (VCS metadata, multi-GB perf output, editor/agent state).

# --- version control & CI metadata -----------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- agent / editor / IDE state (never in an image, may hold local notes) ---
.opencode
.idea
.vscode
.Claude
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- build outputs (rebuilt inside the image; must not leak host binaries) --
bin/
# Pre-built host binaries left at the repo root by local `go build` runs.
# These are darwin/arm64 and must never end up in a linux image layer.
/mcpmock
/perfserver
coverage/
*.out
*.html
*.test

# --- performance corpus: test/perf held ~GBs of k6 output (TASK-030 brief) --
test/perf/

# --- test assets & fixtures not needed to compile the binary ----------------
test/docker-compose/
testdata/

# --- packaging & docs that do not belong in the build context ---------------
helm/
deploy/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.tgz
*.md
LICENSE

# --- local tooling / scratch ------------------------------------------------
hack/
go.work
go.work.sum
